   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "869d79bb-7384-4325-9ff2-27e2dd1ba33d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.2 Tasa de dosis vs distancia\n",
    "\n",
    "La tasa de dosis se calcula promediando sobre los vóxeles con depósito positivo de cada sección de esfera y escalando a la actividad real. Se expresa en Sv/h para facilitar la comparación con los límites ocupacionales de la ICRP (20 mSv/año para trabajadores expuestos)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "8e522888-90c2-49cd-be77-42d3ffe36550",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1870x770 with 11 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Color = D / D̄ del plano (misma escala en todos los paneles → compara forma lateral).\n",
    "# Texto  = dosis del vóxel (µGy) ± incertidumbre estadística.\n",
    "todos = np.concatenate([(r[\"D\"] / r[\"D\"].mean()).ravel() for p in datos.values() for r in p.values()])\n",
    "vmin, vmax = todos.min(), todos.max()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axs = plt.subplots(len(datos), len(DISTANCIAS), figsize=(3.4 * len(DISTANCIAS), 3.5 * len(datos)),\n",
    "                        squeeze=False)\n",
    "for i, (cont, por_d) in enumerate(datos.items()):\n",
    "    for j, d in enumerate(DISTANCIAS):\n",
    "        ax = axs[i][j]\n",
    "        if d not in por_d: ax.axis(\"off\"); continue\n",
    "        r = por_d[d]; D = r[\"D\"]; n = D.shape[0]; h = r[\"lado\"] / 2\n",
    "        patron = D / D.mean()\n",
    "        im = ax.imshow(patron, origin=\"lower\", extent=[-h, h, -h, h], cmap=CMAP_AZUL,\n",
    "                       vmin=vmin, vmax=vmax)\n",
    "        paso = r[\"lado\"] / n\n",
    "        cen = (np.arange(n) + 0.5) * paso - h\n",
    "        for a in range(n):          # a = índice Z (fila), b = índice Y (columna)\n",
    "            for b in range(n):\n",
    "                claro = (patron[a, b] - vmin) / (vmax - vmin) > 0.55\n",
    "                ax.text(cen[b], cen[a], f\"{D[a, b]*1e6:.3g}\\n±{100*r['u'][a, b]:.0f}%\",\n",
    "                        ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=8, color=\"white\" if claro else TINTA)\n",
    "        ax.set_title(f\"{cont.split()[0]} · {d} mm\", fontsize=10)\n",
    "        ax.set_xticks(np.round(cen)); ax.set_yticks(np.round(cen)); ax.grid(False)\n",
    "        ax.tick_params(labelsize=7)\n",
    "        if i == len(datos) - 1: ax.set_xlabel(\"Y (mm)\")\n",
    "        if j == 0: ax.set_ylabel(\"Z (mm)\")\n",
    "cb = fig.colorbar(im, ax=axs, shrink=0.8, pad=0.015); cb.set_label(\"D / D̄ del plano\")\n",
    "fig.suptitle(\"Dosis por vóxel (µGy, 100 mCi · 1 h) y forma lateral del campo\", y=1.0)\n",
    "fig.savefig(\"fig_mapas_calor.png\", dpi=200, bbox_inches=\"tight\"); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "31b49c83-fd54-4e2a-9ccc-dba2da076f6f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.4 Atenuación a través del blindaje\n",
    "#### Perfil de dosis vs posición\n",
    "\n",
    "Muestra cómo decae la dosis al atravesar cada capa del blindaje desde la fuente hasta `det_torso` a 15 cm de la superficie. En general se verá mucho ruido en el exterior del blindaje si se mantiene la emulación con primarios entorno a los cien millones."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1569baf-6574-4678-a377-8493b6973667",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3.3 Modelo teórico: Point-Kernel\n",
    "\n",
    "El modelo analítico Point-Kernel estima la tasa de dosis equivalente ambiental H*(10) a una distancia $r$ del centro del contenedor como:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\dot{H}(r) = \\Gamma_\\delta \\cdot \\frac{A}{r^2} \\cdot e^{-\\sum_i \\mu_i x_i}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "donde:\n",
    "- $\\Gamma_\\delta(\\text{F-18}) = 0.135\\ \\mu\\text{Sv·m}^2\\text{·MBq}^{-1}\\text{·h}^{-1}$\n",
    "- $A = 100\\ \\text{mCi} = 3700\\ \\text{MBq}$\n",
    "- $\\mu_i, x_i$ — coeficiente de atenuación lineal y espesor de la capa $i$\n",
    "- $r$ — distancia desde el centro del contenedor (m)\n",
    "\n",
    "| Material  | $\\mu$ (cm⁻¹) |\n",
    "|-----------|-------------|\n",
    "| Agua      | 0.0966      |\n",
    "| Vidrio    | 0.112       |\n",
    "| Aire      | 0.000112    |\n",
    "| Plomo     | 1.781       |\n",
    "| Acero     | 0.624       |\n",
    "| Tungsteno | 2.402       |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "b22578a1-a53b-4e05-89ae-dd338965032c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1870x506 with 3 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Cada plano solo tiene 9 vóxeles, así que se agrupan los 5 planos de cada contenedor.\n",
    "def vox_arrays(cont):\n",
    "    dosis, patron, unc = [], [], []\n",
    "    for d, r in sorted(datos[cont].items()):\n",
    "        D = r[\"D\"]; n = D.shape[0]; c = (np.arange(n) + 0.5) * r[\"lado\"] / n - r[\"lado\"] / 2\n",
    "        Y, Z = np.meshgrid(c, c)                           # filas = Z, columnas = Y\n",
    "        q = D * (d ** 2 + Y ** 2 + Z ** 2)                 # D·r²: quita la geometría 1/r²\n",
    "        q = q / q[n // 2, n // 2]                          # respecto al vóxel central\n",
    "        mask = np.ones_like(q, bool); mask[n // 2, n // 2] = False\n",
    "        dosis += list(D.ravel() * 1e6); patron += list(q[mask]); unc += list(100 * r[\"u\"].ravel())\n",
    "    return np.array(dosis), np.array(patron), np.array(unc)\n",
    "\n",
    "V = {cont: vox_arrays(cont) for cont in datos if datos[cont]}\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(17, 4.6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# (a) dosis por vóxel, bins logarítmicos comunes\n",
    "todas = np.concatenate([v[0] for v in V.values()])\n",
    "bins = np.logspace(np.log10(todas.min()), np.log10(todas.max()), 14)\n",
    "for cont, (dosis, _, _) in V.items():\n",
    "    ax[0].hist(dosis, bins=bins, color=COLORES[cont], alpha=0.6, edgecolor=\"white\", lw=0.8, label=cont)\n",
    "ax[0].set(xscale=\"log\", xlabel=\"Dosis por vóxel (µGy)\", ylabel=\"N.º de vóxeles\",\n",
    "          title=\"(a) Distribución de dosis\"); ax[0].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# (b) caída lateral: D·r² del vóxel / D·r² del centro (1 = sin caída)\n",
    "bins_b = np.linspace(min(v[1].min() for v in V.values()) * 0.98, 1.0, 12)\n",
    "for cont, (_, pat, _) in V.items():\n",
    "    ax[1].hist(pat, bins=bins_b, color=COLORES[cont], alpha=0.6, edgecolor=\"white\", lw=0.8, label=cont)\n",
    "    ax[1].axvline(np.median(pat), color=COLORES[cont], lw=1.5, ls=\"--\")\n",
    "ax[1].set(xlabel=\"D·r² (vóxel) / D·r² (centro)\", ylabel=\"N.º de vóxeles\",\n",
    "          title=\"(b) Caída lateral (líneas = mediana)\"); ax[1].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# (c) calidad estadística\n",
    "tope = max(100, max(v[2].max() for v in V.values()))\n",
    "bins_c = np.linspace(0, min(tope, 100), 21)\n",
    "for cont, (_, _, unc) in V.items():\n",
    "    ax[2].hist(np.clip(unc, 0, 100), bins=bins_c, color=COLORES[cont], alpha=0.6, edgecolor=\"white\",\n",
    "               lw=0.8, label=f\"{cont} · {np.mean(unc <= 100*UMBRAL_INCERT)*100:.0f} % ≤ 10 %\")\n",
    "ax[2].axvline(100 * UMBRAL_INCERT, color=TINTA, lw=1.2, ls=\"--\")\n",
    "ax[2].text(100 * UMBRAL_INCERT + 0.5, ax[2].get_ylim()[1] * 0.92, \"criterio 10 %\", fontsize=9, color=TINTA)\n",
    "ax[2].set(xlabel=\"Incertidumbre estadística por vóxel (%)\", ylabel=\"N.º de vóxeles\",\n",
    "          title=\"(c) Calidad estadística\"); ax[2].legend()\n",
    "fig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(\"fig_histogramas.png\", dpi=200, bbox_inches=\"tight\"); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
